## Original Content
A new survey shows even a $500 unexpected expense may throw households off track when it comes to big life goals like saving for retirement.

## Summary
A new survey shows that even a $500 unexpected expense can significantly disrupt working households' ability to achieve major financial goals like saving for retirement. Financial expert Suze Orman warns that this shortfall signals danger for financial stability among these households.

## Key Points
- The survey indicates that many working households lack sufficient emergency savings to handle unexpected costs.
- A $500 unexpected expense is enough to derail progress towards big life goals, particularly retirement savings.
- This situation highlights the financial vulnerability and precarity of working households.
- Suze Orman emphasizes the urgency of addressing this issue to prevent long-term financial hardship.


